course: dictionary
lesson: 15406
title: Spots: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Spots can be a thing you can see, or an action someone does. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: «The leopard has black spots on its golden fur.» Here spots are marks, so the word is a noun. «Ella spots a mistake in her spelling.» Here spots is a verb: Ella notices the mistake.
explain: «Sam came out in red spots after he caught chickenpox.» These spots are small red bumps on the skin. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Spots as a noun can mean small round marks, small red bumps on the skin, or places.
fact: Spots as a verb means notices or sees something, often something that is hard to see.
fact: «On the spot» means right away, or right there.
fact: «A tight spot» means a difficult situation.
fact: Spots on the skin can be a sign of an illness, such as chickenpox or measles.
exercise: «The ladybird has seven black spots on its red back.» What are the spots? | Mistakes that the ladybird made | Red bumps from an illness | Places where ladybirds like to sleep | *Small round marks of a different colour
exercise: Ben says, «I spot a fox behind the tree.» What does spots mean here? | Places where foxes live | Small red bumps on his skin | *Sees something, often something hard to see | Small round marks on the tree
exercise: The doctor says Mia has spots on her arms and must rest at home. What might the spots be a sign of? | A parking ticket | *An illness like chickenpox | A new pattern for her shirt | Dirt from playing in the garden
test: «The shop manager fixed the broken toy on the spot.» What does on the spot mean? | Very slowly | Under the table | *Right away | Next week
test: «We were in a tight spot when the bus broke down.» What does a tight spot mean? | *A difficult situation | A kind of game | A small, narrow shop | A comfy place to sit
exam: In «Lee spots two spots on the rug», which option is correct? | Both spots mean small red bumps | The first spots means small marks, and the second spots means notices | *The first spots means notices, and the second spots means small marks | Both spots mean places
